  "published": "2026-07-07T11:44:06.563Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.0.0 — BREAKING. See MIGRATION.md. Breaking API: (1) the `enableConsoleLogging` parameter is removed from both `AddStepUpLogging(...)` overloads — console output is now driven solely by `StepUpLoggingOptions.EnableConsoleLogging`. (2) The `configure` delegate changed from `Action<HostBuilderContext, IServiceProvider, LoggerConfiguration>` to `Action<IServiceProvider, LoggerConfiguration>`; the synthesized fake `HostBuilderContext` (with null Configuration/HostingEnvironment) is gone, removing an NRE risk — resolve `IConfiguration`/`IHostEnvironment` from the `IServiceProvider` instead. Breaking behavior: (3) config-declared `Serilog:WriteTo` sinks now sit behind the step-up LevelSwitch instead of exporting everything at Verbose from the Verbose root; use the immediate (`IsImmediate`) / request-summary (`IsRequestSummary`) bypass for always-on export. Also carried in this release (non-breaking): removed the reflective DiagnosticContext registration; the bypass logger is now disposed on shutdown so its async buffers flush; the File sink is shared.",
